### Test 1: Successful Login (Get JWT Token)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

###

### Test 2: Access Protected Endpoint Without Token (Should Fail)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Test 3: Access Protected Endpoint With Invalid Token (Should Fail)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_xyz
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Test 4: Access Protected Endpoint With Valid Token (Should Succeed)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJqb2huLmRvZUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInVzZXJJZCI6IjU1MGU4NDAwLWUyOWItNDFkNC1hNzE2LTQ0NjY1NTQ0MDAwMCIsInRva2VuVHlwZSI6ImFjY2VzcyIsImlhdCI6MTcwODEwODgwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzA4MTA5NzAwfQ.signature
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Test 5: Register New User (Public Endpoint)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "password": "AnotherSecure456"
}

###

### Test 6: Login with Newly Registered User
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "password": "AnotherSecure456"
}

###

